Vision North Somerset is an independent local charity who receive a grant from North Somerset Council to deliver the statutory services:
•	vision rehabilitation (for example mobility and daily living skills, home adaption advice) ;
•	hearing equipment (advice on and fitting of equipment to help with doorbells, telephones, television) ;
•	equipment for people with visual impairment ;
•	information, advice and guidance including local referrals.

The charity also fundraises to provide: 
•	Technology training for visually impaired people (for example mobile phones, tablet computers and smart speakers) ;
•	A range of social inclusion activities from befriending and support groups to physical activities such as swimming and lawn bowls.

Founded in 1988 by parents of children with heart disorders, the Wessex Children's Heart Circle is run entirely by voluntary help and donations. The Wessex Children's Heart Circle aims to support children with heart disorders and their families whilst they undergo the traumas of discovery of a heart problem and subsequent surgery or other treatment, on-going permanent problems, or, sadly, sometimes bereavement. We provide support in a number of ways: 

By putting members in touch with other families who have similar problems; By providing information concerning the experience of hospitalisation; 

By providing practical help to families and offering limited financial help at times of hospitalisation; 

By fund raising to provide hospital equipment and other items to make life more comfortable for children during their stay at the Centre; 

By funding cardiac research. There is close liaison between our Circle and the cardiologists and surgeons at Southampton General Hospital so that funds are used effectively.

Breakthrough UK's mission is to promote the rights, responsibilities and respect of disabled people.

Influencing government, local, regional and national agencies about barriers to disabled people's participation;
Enabling disabled people to pursue and develop their careers;
Providing greater choice, control and independent living; and
Working towards being financially stable, politically aware with healthy growth.
